## Exciting times ahead
We don't have all the necessary tools, **yet**. Some SAR operations over Sentinel-1 data are not possible, **yet**. But the path that `.zarr` is forging has already shaken the Copernicus Sentinel world, with no way back!

Libraries like [sarsen](https://github.com/bopen/sarsen) are already enabling steps toward a fully cloud-native, Python-based SAR processing workflow. The open source community is gradually recreating complex SAR operations that once seemed only possible using applications like SNAP over the `.SAFE` format. **And these are great news!**

As an Earth Observation and Geo-Data Science student, discovering and learning about `.zarr` and its capabilities was incredibly valuable. I started as one of the EOPF 101 users and, step by step, came to understand the positive impact that the Sentinel `.zarr` conversion will have from now on. Above all, it is exciting to realize that these changes were motivated, driven and developed by the open-source community. And anyone can be a part of it! The next big contributions on the cloud-native SAR processing workflows might come from me, you or any other EOPF 101 user!

